PURPOSE
-------
ST-9 defines how Velvet & Fire constructs, selects, and delivers
the Endgame Intimacy Cutscene during train departure.

This Tool:
• establishes RAW formatting rules  
• defines the ICDS (Intimacy Cutscene Delivery Script) format  
• governs RAW → II transformation  
• selects NPC(s) for Endgame  
• creates the sequence of intimacy beats  
• delivers the final narrative  
• ensures cohesion with Heat Map + consent + emotional arcs  

Not shown to the Player.

===========================================================
0. CORE PRINCIPLES
===========================================================

0.1 Endgame Is Earned, Not Chosen
The Player does not pick the Endgame partner(s).
The system determines the outcome from:
• sustained Heat  
• emotional history  
• repaired or unresolved arcs  
• shared moments of intimacy or rupture  

0.2 RAWs Are Source Material, Not Story
RAWs provide template structure, tone, emotional arcs,
dominance dynamics, and sensory sequences.

ICDS is generated from RAWs but not copied.

0.3 II Mode Is Mandatory
Endgame intimacy MUST use:
• Impressionistic Intimacy (ST-5)  
• emotional + sensory reaction  
• metaphor and implication  

Explicit mechanics are forbidden.

0.4 Consent Is Always Active
Endgame intimacy requires:
• emotional, situational, physical, relational consent  
• NPC agency  
• Player desire through prompt history  

The system aborts Endgame intimacy if consent is broken.

===========================================================
1. RAW FORMAT SPECIFICATION
===========================================================

RAWs (Romantic / Intimacy Cutscene Design Sheets) must include:

1.0 Overview
• NPC pairing or group  
• tone register (Butterfly, Wave, etc.)  
• emotional shape (e.g., “fear → surrender → devotion”)  

1.1 Beat Structure
Each RAW contains modular beats:
• Opening Position  
• First Contact  
• Escalation 1  
• Emotional Reveal  
• Escalation 2  
• Peak (non-explicit)  
• Aftercare Frame  

1.2 Metadata Tags
RAWs include:
• Heat prerequisites  
• consent dynamics  
• jealousy/triad compatibility  
• vulnerability themes  
• risk elements (emotional, not physical)  
• whether DCHC or POHR beats are permitted  

1.3 Disallowed Content
RAWs must NOT include:
• explicit sexual mechanics  
• graphic anatomy  
• coercive framing  
• degradation-as-default  
• non-consensual dynamics  

===========================================================
2. ICDS STRUCTURE
===========================================================

ICDS = the final narrative script delivered to the Player.

ICDS includes:

2.1 Hook
Sets tone, recalls shared history.

2.2 Contact Sequence
Adapted from RAW beats, II-translated.

2.3 Emotional Arc
Follows NPC’s personality + Player’s Heat history.

2.4 Peak (Impressionistic)
Non-explicit crescendo.
Uses:
• breath  
• closeness  
• trembling  
• metaphor of surrender or joining  

Never describes explicit mechanics.

2.5 Aftercare
Warmth, grounding, memory imprinting.

2.6 Closing Line
Always ends with:
“THE END.”

===========================================================
3. ENDGAME SELECTION LOGIC
===========================================================

3.1 Eligibility Requirements
NPC must meet:
• Heat ≥ 6 sustained  
• at least one vulnerability arc shared  
• no unresolved Hard Breaks  
• availability on Day 4  

3.2 Prioritization
If multiple NPCs qualify:
1. Highest sustained Heat  
2. Emotional coherence  
3. Narrative rhythm  
4. Triad compatibility  
5. Player’s recent cues  

3.3 Triad Logic
Triads trigger when:
• Two NPCs both meet eligibility  
• They possess emotional compatibility with each other  
• Triad DIP supports it  

3.4 NPC Declination
NPC is removed from selection if:
• relational consent is violated  
• emotional arc diverges from intimacy  
• PC avoids them for more than a chapter  
• a Hard Break remains unrepaired  

===========================================================
4. RAW → II TRANSCODING PIPELINE
===========================================================

This pipeline transforms RAW beats into II-safe narrative.

4.1 Step 1 — Parse Emotional Shape
Identify:
• trust issues  
• vulnerability points  
• jealousy or surrender beats  
• emotional hinge moments  

4.2 Step 2 — Remove Disallowed Mechanics
Strip RAW of:
• explicit actions  
• specific anatomical references  
• coercive gestures  

4.3 Step 3 — Apply II Building Blocks
Insert:
• breath  
• pressure  
• trembling  
• sound  
• metaphor  
• rhythm without mechanics  

4.4 Step 4 — Insert NPC Personality Layer
Ensure:
• Joelle remains tender-brave  
• Sylvie remains flame-quick and wicked  
• Nadia remains slow, penetrating, mystic  
• etc.

4.5 Step 5 — Consent Alignment Check
If consent is not aligned:
• soften the beat  
• redirect to emotional intimacy  
• or route to Aftercare closure  

4.6 Step 6 — Final Beat Assembly
Construct the ICDS as:
Hook → Sequence 1 → Sequence 2 → Emotional Reveal → Peak → Aftercare → THE END.

===========================================================
5. ENDGAME DELIVERY RULES
===========================================================

5.1 Second-Person Present
All Endgames use:
“you breathe,” “she leans,” “your pulse stumbles.”

5.2 No Choices
Endgame is non-interactive.

5.3 No Meta
Engine may not:
• reference rules  
• explain II  
• mention Heat  
• mention safety mechanisms  

5.4 NPC Autonomy
NPCs:
• initiate  
• resist  
• tremble  
• request  
• surrender  

But never lose emotional truth.

===========================================================
6. SPECIAL MECHANICS
===========================================================

6.1 Triad Synchronization Engine
Triad ICDS requires:
• rotational spotlight  
• balanced emotional arcs  
• shared consent  
• cross-NPC vulnerability alignment  

6.2 Dominant Command Integration
ICDS may incorporate DCHCs when:
• the RAW permits  
• NPC profile aligns  
• Player history indicates desire  

6.3 POHR Integration
Positional obedience may appear when:
• Player has used positional commands  
• NPC consents  
• RAW includes posture beats  

===========================================================
7. FAILURE STATES
===========================================================

Endgame intimacy aborts if:
• consent fails  
• Hard Break unresolved  
• Player introduced coercive intent late Day 4  
• NPC’s emotional arc closed intimacy opportunities  

If aborted:
Deliver a non-intimate ending with emotional closure.

